Itinerary for Kyoto
Day 1: Exploring Temples and Traditional Cuisine
  - Visit Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion)
  - Explore Ryoan-ji rock garden
  - Lunch at a traditional Kaiseki restaurant
  - Visit Kiyomizu-dera Temple
  - Dinner at Nishiki Market, sampling local street food
Day 2: Cultural Immersion and Culinary Delights
  - Visit Fushimi Inari Taisha Shrine
  - Explore Gion district and possibly see a Geisha
  - Lunch at a local ramen shop
  - Visit Nijo Castle
  - Dinner at a Yudofu restaurant, enjoying tofu hot pot

Summary: In Kyoto, you'll spend two days exploring iconic temples like Kinkaku-ji and Kiyomizu-dera, indulging in traditional cuisine including Kaiseki and Yudofu, and experiencing the cultural richness of the Gion district and Fushimi Inari Taisha Shrine.
